<title>USA: Columbia/HCA hospital violated labor law - NYT.</title>
<headline>Columbia/HCA hospital violated labor law - NYT.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>An administrative law judge ruled a Kentucky hospital owned by Columbia/HCA Healthcare Corp violated federal labor laws by trying to stop nurses from forming a union, the New York Times said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The judge found Audubon Regional Medical Center of Louisville, Ky. engaged in unfair labor practices through threats and retaliatory actions taken against nurses who supported the union, the paper said.</p>
<p>The company was not immediately available to comment.</p>
<p>((New York newsdesk 212-859-1610))</p>
